  "notes": "Cash basis audit. Governmental: one fund (General), p4. Beginning cash not printed (fund balance 237,562 and prior period adjustment 68,765 recorded as printed, p4). Ending cash = General Fund total assets (cash at bank + county treasurer) p3; p3 cash at bank 367,356 = p1 governmental cash at bank 331,870 + Cash - ARPA 35,486. Business-type from the cash-basis proprietary statement Total column (p6); receipts total = Total operating revenues 650,524; disbursements total 639,369 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2) = operating expenses 532,464 + nonoperating debt service 106,905; beginning net position 193,522 restated by prior period adjustment 87,970 to 281,492. The only supplementary schedule is the combined all-funds budgetary comparison (p7; its Budget and Actual column headings appear swapped), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental (p4) and proprietary (p6) statements, as in FY2023; Water and Sewer expenditure detail totals add nonoperating debt service to total operating expenses (computed). Grants & contributions 42,990 kept as one line (SoA p2: 35,486 General Government + 7,504 Culture & Recreation; ARPA cash 35,486 on p1; no printed grant/contribution split). Balance sheet: governmental funds statement (p3, equals government-wide governmental 369,398) plus proprietary statement of net position (p5); totals 662,165 printed on p1. Read pages 1-7 of 7"
